course: dictionary
lesson: 11810
title: Biblical: from the Bible, or very big
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Biblical is a describing word, an adjective. It has two meanings. The first is to do with the Bible, or found in it. «The class read a biblical story about Noah and the ark.» The clue is the Bible: a biblical story comes from the Bible.
explain: The second meaning is informal, used for exaggeration. «The rain was biblical, falling in sheets all afternoon.» Nobody means a flood from the Bible here. The word tells you the rain was enormous. Ask yourself: is this about the Bible, or is it just really big? The sentence will tell you which.
explain: Look for the phrases biblical often goes with: biblical times, a biblical story, of biblical proportions. «Our teacher said the village was built in biblical times» means long ago, in the days of the Bible. Swap in your meaning and check that it still makes sense.
fact: «Biblical» means to do with the Bible or found in the Bible.
fact: «Biblical» can also mean very great or huge, as in «rain of biblical proportions».
fact: The informal meaning is a joke or exaggeration, so it is used in relaxed, everyday speech.
fact: Context clues, the words around a word, tell you which meaning fits.
fact: Biblical times means the days described in the Bible.
exercise: «Noah's ark is a biblical story.» What does biblical mean here? | Very huge | *To do with the Bible | Very cold | Very tasty
exercise: «The flood was biblical, and the streets were under water for days.» What does biblical mean here? | *Enormous, very great | Very small and neat | Very quiet and calm | Something you eat at lunch
exercise: «The class learned about biblical times in RE lessons.» Find and copy the word that describes the times. | class | learned | *biblical | lessons
test: «The children read a biblical story about David and Goliath.» What does biblical mean? | Very tiny | Very loud noise | Something you eat at lunch | *Something from the Bible
test: «The queue for the new ride was of biblical proportions.» What does biblical mean? | Very short | Very hot | To do with a church | *Enormous, huge
exam: Which sentence uses biblical to mean huge? | *«The storm was biblical, with rain for days.» | «We read a biblical story at school.» | «Biblical times were long ago.» | «Our teacher is reading a biblical tale.»
